BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 506 Td (Large Language Models \(LLMs\) have achieved remarkable conversational fluency across) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 493 Td (general domains. However, in enterprise, academic, and mission-critical workflows,) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 480 Td (standalone parametric models suffer from severe architectural limitations: \(1\) Knowledge) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 467 Td (Cutoffs, where models cannot access information post-training; \(2\) Hallucinations, where) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 454 Td (models invent plausible falsehoods in low-resource or proprietary niches; and \(3\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 441 Td (Absence of Provenance, where generated text lacks traceable evidence or citations.) Tj ET
0.18 0.22 0.28 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 423 Td (Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\), formulated by Lewis et al. \(2020\), bridges this) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 410 Td (divide by decoupling factual knowledge storage from linguistic generation. By querying a) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 397 Td (non-parametric dense vector index of external documents, RAG conditions the generative) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 384 Td (LLM strictly upon retrieved factual passages, providing verified citations, real-time) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 50 371 Td (updatability, and near-zero hallucination rates.) Tj ET
